[
  {
    "sha": "ac345f1c0cf402a9c26363f675196fab32c8bd8e",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGFjMzQ1ZjFjMGNmNDAyYTljMjYzNjNmNjc1MTk2ZmFiMzJjOGJkOGU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-24T00:17:31Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-24T00:17:31Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): return the rotaries to zero at program end (Fanuc, Doosan DNM)\n\nA program whose last section is tilted ended with the table or the head\nat the last tilt after M30. The Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts now end such\na program with the same blocks as the return of #3466: G49, the Z\nretract, G90, the zero angle words with no X/Y word, then an\nincremental X/Y home (G91 G28 X0 Y0) and M30. Doosan unclamps (M11)\nand clamps (M10) a turning A around the return. With safeRetract G53\nthe program writes G53 Z, then the zero angles. An upright program\nends byte for byte as before.\n\nThe catalog program multiaxis/indexed changes in its last blocks only.\n\nFixes #3540\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
